@page "/About"
@model FinGuardLite.Pages.AboutModel

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About FinGuard Lite";
}

<div class="mb-4">
    <h1>About FinGuard Lite</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">
        A student-built fintech risk monitoring prototype for simulated transaction screening, alert review, and audit traceability.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">Project Purpose</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>
            FinGuard Lite is a portfolio project built to demonstrate how financial technology systems can support
            transaction risk monitoring, alert review, and audit logging.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            In a real financial institution, transaction data would usually be ingested from banking, card,
            payment, or AML monitoring systems. Since this is a student prototype without access to real bank data,
            the project uses mock customers and simulated transactions to test the risk scoring workflow.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">How the Prototype Works</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li>Mock customer profiles are created to represent customer master or KYC-style data.</li>
            <li>Transactions are simulated manually or generated through the database seeder.</li>
            <li>The system calculates a risk score for each transaction using rule-based checks.</li>
            <li>Medium and high-risk transactions are flagged as risk alerts.</li>
            <li>Risk analysts can review alerts and update their status.</li>
            <li>Audit logs record key actions for traceability.</li>
            <li>Role-based demo login controls what each user type can access.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">Demo Roles</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <table class="table table-bordered table-striped mb-0">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Role</th>
                    <th>Access</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Risk Analyst</td>
                    <td>Dashboard, Customers, Transactions, Risk Alerts</td>
                    <td>Reviews simulated transaction activity and investigates flagged alerts.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Compliance Officer</td>
                    <td>Dashboard, About, Audit Logs</td>
                    <td>Reviews system traceability and checks whether key actions are recorded.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Admin</td>
                    <td>Full access</td>
                    <td>Has access to all prototype functions for demonstration and testing.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">Risk Scoring Rules</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <table class="table table-bordered table-striped mb-0">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Rule</th>
                    <th>Condition</th>
                    <th>Score Added</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>High Transaction Amount</td>
                    <td>Amount is $5,000 or above</td>
                    <td>+30</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Very High Transaction Amount</td>
                    <td>Amount is $10,000 or above</td>
                    <td>+50</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Overseas Transaction</td>
                    <td>Transaction country is not Singapore</td>
                    <td>+15</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Unknown Merchant</td>
                    <td>Merchant is recorded as Unknown</td>
                    <td>+15</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>High-Risk Category</td>
                    <td>Crypto, Gambling, Unknown, or Money Transfer</td>
                    <td>+25</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Income Mismatch</td>
                    <td>Transaction amount exceeds 50% of customer's monthly income</td>
                    <td>+25</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Repeated Transactions</td>
                    <td>Customer makes multiple transactions in one day</td>
                    <td>+20</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">Dataset and Assumptions</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>
            The application uses a mock five-year transaction dataset from 2022 to 2026. This makes the prototype
            more realistic than a one-day dataset while keeping the number of records manageable for demonstration.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            The transaction records, customer profiles, risk alerts, and audit logs are not real financial data.
            They are generated for learning, testing, and portfolio demonstration purposes only.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
    <div class="card-header bg-white">
        <h5 class="mb-0">Limitations and Future Improvements</h5>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>
            FinGuard Lite is not a production fraud detection or AML system. It does not connect to real banking APIs,
            real-time payment systems, customer onboarding platforms, or machine learning models.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            Future improvements could include search and filtering, charts, CSV export, API-based transaction ingestion,
            stronger authentication, cloud deployment, and more advanced risk scoring logic.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>